Input: {"question": "Which country is Chintamani Acharya a citizen of?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 22, "text": "**Chintamani Acharya**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 24, "end": 165, "text": "Chintamani Acharya (born 1885) is an Indian lawyer and writer, best known for his literary contributions to the Indian independence movement."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 166, "end": 280, "text": "However, what is lesser known about Acharya is his unique citizenship status as a citizen of the Kingdom of Italy."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 281, "end": 309, "text": "**Early Life and Education**"}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 311, "end": 382, "text": "Acharya was born in Bombay, British India, to a family of modest means."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 383, "end": 546, "text": "Despite the challenges he faced, Acharya's intellectual prowess and passion for learning earned him a scholarship to study law at the University of Turin in Italy."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 547, "end": 708, "text": "It was during his time in Italy that Acharya developed a deep appreciation for the country's culture and history, which would later influence his literary works."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 709, "end": 736, "text": "**Citizenship Controversy**"}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 738, "end": 921, "text": "In 1905, Acharya's application for Italian citizenship was approved by King Victor Emmanuel III, making him one of the first Indians to be granted citizenship of the Kingdom of Italy."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 922, "end": 1052, "text": "This decision was met with controversy, as some argued that Acharya's Indian heritage made him ineligible for Italian citizenship."}, 